{"name":"Night Club","hex":"#494b4e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night club","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of nightclub."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night_club"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nightclub","blocks":[{"text":"A nightclub or dance club is a venue that is open at night, usually for drinking, dancing and other entertainment. Nightclubs often have a bar and discotheque with a dance floor, laser lighting displays, and a stage for live music or a disc jockey (DJ) who mixes recorded music. Nightclubs tend to be smaller than live music venues like theatres and stadiums, with few or no seats for customers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg/330px-Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightclub","wikidata":"Q622425"},{"title":"Night Club (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Club is an American electronic band, formed by Mark Brooks and Emily Kavanaugh in 2012. The band is from Los Angeles, California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Night_Club_2015.jpg/330px-Night_Club_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Club_(band)","wikidata":"Q7033251"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg/500px-Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg/500px-Wikipedia_space_ibiza%2803%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWikipedia_space_ibiza(03).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Berlin_Joachimsthaler_Stra%C3%9Fe_191-0462.jpg/500px-Berlin_Joachimsthaler_Stra%C3%9Fe_191-0462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Berlin_Joachimsthaler_Stra%C3%9Fe_191-0462.jpg/500px-Berlin_Joachimsthaler_Stra%C3%9Fe_191-0462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"Kakadu\" (1919–1937), a Pre-World War II nightclub in Berlin,[17] offered a bar, a dance floor, live music played by jazz band, and cabaret.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerlin_Joachimsthaler_Stra%C3%9Fe_191-0462.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Dj2can_club_dj.jpg/330px-Dj2can_club_dj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Dj2can_club_dj.jpg/330px-Dj2can_club_dj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A disc jockey (DJ) mixing vinyl records on turntables (Inland Empire, 2009)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADj2can_club_dj.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t